        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Altar frontal embroidered with scenes of the Baptism of Christ and the Virgin and Child in the main part. Cloth of embroidered silk velvet in gold, silver, silver-gilt and silk threads in split, brick and satin stitches with couched and applied work.\n\nIn the centre of the upper band is Christ carrying the Cross, and is flanked by the eagle symbol for St John the Evangelist on either side. On the extreme left is the martyrdom of St John the Evangelist, and on the extreme right is St John the Evangelist with the angels.\n\nThe side borders shows St Francis receiving his wounds, and St Catherine of Siena."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/11167d50-8fc5-3536-a272-50cbcf47e99b> .

